(4580793, 659333, 88054, '<td valign="top">I think I would have preferred a color photo. I''m guessing the grass is a golden brown and the sky is a deep blue with wispy white clouds. Still like it though. Good luck.</td>', 'I think I would have preferred a color photo. I''m guessing the grass is a golden brown and the sky is a deep blue with wispy white clouds. Still like it though. Good luck.', '2008-03-23 00:11:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(4580801, 658567, 88054, '<td valign="top">This is a great photo. I like the perspective and the colors of the moss. Did you try it with a deeper depth of field? The branches to the right and the tree in the background are a little distracting to me. Perhaps if they were way out of focus (Very shallow DOF) or in sharp focus (Deep DOF) I would appriciate the textures more.</td>', 'This is a great photo. I like the perspective and the colors of the moss. Did you try it with a deeper depth of field? The branches to the right and the tree in the background are a little distracting to me. Perhaps if they were way out of focus (Very shallow DOF) or in sharp focus (Deep DOF) I would appriciate the textures more.', '2008-03-23 00:19:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(4580807, 658648, 88054, '<td valign="top">I like the general feel and composition of the photo, however; the textures are flat. Minimum shadows on the grasses in the foreground. The fence posts are not close enough to see the weathered wood grain. I would have liked to see the first fence post very close to the camera. Maybe even on one knee looking up the hill so we could see the grass better. All that said...Its difficult to get contrasting colors with a black and white photo under a mid day sun. Good luck.</td>', 'I like the general feel and composition of the photo, however; the textures are flat. Minimum shadows on the grasses in the foreground. The fence posts are not close enough to see the weathered wood grain. I would have liked to see the first fence post very close to the camera. Maybe even on one knee looking up the hill so we could see the grass better. All that said...Its difficult to get contrasting colors with a black and white photo under a mid day sun. Good luck.', '2008-03-23 00:30:22.000000', NULL, 1),
